```text
CHEYENNE
Police
Protecting the legend...
415 W. 18th Street • Cheyenne, WY 82001 • Phone (307) 637-6500 • Fax (307) 637-6558 • www.cheyennepd.org
TO:
DATE:  January 8, 2020
FROM:
Honorable Mayor Orr and City Council
Brian N. Kozak, Chief of Police
SUBJECT:
Staff Report to Adopt an Ordinance Amending Chapters 8.40, Food and Food Service
Establishments, within Title 8, Health and Safety, of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne,
Wyoming, and Chapters 10.12, Administration and Enforcement, 10.16, Arrest and Citation Procedure,
10.52, Stopping, Standing and Parking Generally, 10.60, Parking Limitations, 10.64, Loading and
Unloading, 10.68, Critical Traffic and Parking Areas, within Title 10, Vehicles and Traffic, of the City of
Cheyenne Municipal Code.
RECOMMENDATION
Staff recommends that the City Council consider the proposed ordinance to amend Municipal Code provisions
to update ordinances and definitions involving parking. The amendments are related to: food service parking,
impound illegally parked vehicles, immobilization, illegally parked vehicles, failure to comply with parking
citation, presumption in reference to illegal parking, request for hearing, operator error, prohibited in specified
places, diagonal parking permits, downtown construction parking, signed time limitations, notice of violation,
fine schedule, curb loading zones, procedures for establishment of critical parking area, and downtown
residential parking.  The ordinance intends to improve the management and effectiveness of the City of
Cheyenne public parking.  The complete ordinance amendment is attached to this staff report as Exhibit “A”.
BACKGROUND
In the spring of 2016, the Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization engaged Kimley-Horn and Associates
to develop a Strategic Parking Management Plan for Downtown Cheyenne, Wyoming.  On March 31, 2017, the
Cheyenne Metropolitan Organization finalized their Downtown Strategic Parking Plan.  The key findings of
what the parking program needed:
1. A more comprehensive and strategic program action plan relative to parking and transportation
policy.
2. Enhanced parking management expertise.
3. Establish parking as a separate “enterprise fund” and dedicate all parking related revenue streams to
support the enterprise fund.
4. A strong customer service orientation.
5. While related to the enhancing parking management expertise and training/staff development, this
focus area is about gaining an in-depth understanding of the many complex and challenging aspects
that are somewhat unique to parking.
6. Investment in New Technology – Leveraging new technology will be a critical element in achieving
many of the stated goals.
